# A widget of several clauses has arguments for its clauses to tell apart. A second block
# for a widget that takes none can never be chosen: written `fn @Twice:` twice the checker
# says `unreachable`; written as two bare blocks it lets the program through today, and
# the back end builds the first (its guard "a widget of several clauses that takes no
# arguments", lower/node/static.prism, stands behind). Written by Claude on the
# claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

@Twice: @unit
@Twice:
    Ui.Label($text=$"one")
@Twice:
    Ui.Label($text=$"two")

@page: @unit
@page:
    @Twice
